# Running the Prospecting CRM — choose a data home

When the user asks to **run**, **start**, **open**, or **launch** the CRM
(prospects / prospecting CRM), do **not** start it against a database blindly.

## 1. Prefer the list picker

Day-to-day launch is **`run-live.bat`**, which starts
`python -m crm serve --open --port 8765 --pick-home`. The browser opens a
home screen under `Documents\`: existing `ProspectingCRM*` folders, plus
**Start a new list**.

If they ask you to start it from chat, check port **8765** first. If it is
free, start with `--pick-home` so they choose in the browser — do not assume
the live list, and **never** create a database inside the git checkout.

Only skip the picker when they explicitly want a **specific home already
named** — set `CRM_HOME` to that folder and start without `--pick-home`.

## 2. After a list is open

- Confirm the path in **Settings** (or `python -m crm status` with the same
  `CRM_HOME`).
- If the app is already running on port 8765, say so; don’t assume a second
  copy is safe without checking.
- Remind first-time / empty ICP users: open **Settings**, fill who they sell
  to (or **Load example ICP**), then use Research.

## 3. Brand-new clone (no .venv yet)

If `.venv` is missing, point them to **`setup.bat`** (Windows) or:

```text
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -e .
```

Do not invent cloud deploy steps. Local only.

## 4. Never

- Never wipe or replace `Documents\ProspectingCRM\data\crm.db` without an
  explicit ask.
- Never run `init-home` in a way that overwrites an existing live DB
  (`init-home` already refuses to overwrite — keep it that way).
- Never treat the git checkout as a calling list. Data belongs in
  `Documents\ProspectingCRM*`, not in `<repo>\data\`.
